## 3. Target Users

House In Hand adopts a **Single Account, Multi-Profile Architecture** for platform users, plus an internal-only **Admin/Staff Role System** for the Admin Console.

### 3.1 Public / Unauthenticated

| Type | Description |
|---|---|
| Website Visitor | Anonymous browser of the public marketing site — landing page, listings preview, blog, FAQs. Not authenticated. Primary conversion target for signup. |

### 3.2 Platform Users (registered, KYC-verified)

Users register once and may create multiple profile types under a single account. Each profile is independently verified and activated through KYC verification.

| Profile Type | Description |
|---|---|
| Student Profile | Users seeking hostel accommodation |
| Tenant Profile | Users renting residential properties |
| Landlord Profile | Property owners managing rentals |
| Estate Manager Profile | Organizations or individuals managing multiple properties |

**Key user notes:**

| Rule | Description |
|---|---|
| Single Account | One user account per individual |
| Multiple Profiles | Users may create multiple profile types |
| One Profile Per Type | Users cannot create two profiles of the same type |
| KYC Mandatory | Every profile requires KYC verification |
| Profile Switching | Users can switch between verified profiles |

### 3.3 Internal Staff (Admin Console)

Admin is **not** a KYC profile type — it's a separate, internal authentication system with its own RBAC.

| Role | Description | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| Content Editor | Manages public website content only | Landing page sections, blog, FAQs, testimonials, media library |
| Ops/KYC Reviewer | Reviews and approves/rejects user KYC and listings | Identity verification, listing verification, fraud reports |
| Super Admin | Full access | All of the above + user management, RBAC config, audit logs |

